Subject:  [patch 166/181] h8300, nds32, openrisc: simplify
 detection of memory extents
Message-ID: <20201013235736.6bejcxbHY%akpm@linux-foundation.org>
In-Reply-To: <20201013164658.3bfd96cc224d8923e66a9f4e@linux-foundation.org>
User-Agent: s-nail v14.8.16
Precedence: bulk
Reply-To: linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org
List-ID: <mm-commits.vger.kernel.org>
X-Mailing-List: mm-commits@vger.kernel.org

From: Mike Rapoport <rppt@linux.ibm.com>
Subject: h8300, nds32, openrisc: simplify detection of memory extents

Instead of traversing memblock.memory regions to find memory_start and
memory_end, simply query memblock_{start,end}_of_DRAM().

Link: https://lkml.kernel.org/r/20200818151634.14343-6-rppt@kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Mike Rapoport <rppt@linux.ibm.com>
Acked-by: Stafford Horne <shorne@gmail.com>
Cc: Andy Lutomirski <luto@kernel.org>
